#: ../../resources_page.rst:128
msgid "Feather icons"
msgstr "Ikoner från Feather"

#: ../../resources_page.rst:130
msgid ""
"A set of open source icons from https://feathericons.com but in a Vector "
"Library form, so it can be easily accessed from inside Krita after the "
"import. Each icon is designed on a 24x24 grid with an emphasis on "
"simplicity, consistency, and flexibility."
msgstr ""

#: ../../resources_page.rst:132
msgid "Link: https://github.com/MiAlmeida/krita-feather"
msgstr "Länk: https://github.com/MiAlmeida/krita-feather"

#: ../../resources_page.rst:136
msgid "Templates"
msgstr "Mallar"

#: ../../resources_page.rst:137
msgid ""
"Templates are .kra files that you can base your new documents on. To learn "
"more see :ref:`create_new_document_from_template`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../resources_page.rst:140
msgid "Storyboard template"
msgstr ""

#: ../../resources_page.rst:142
msgid ""
"The layout and layer setup is inspired by traditional Studio Ghibli "
"storyboards, and Tony Gaddis’ storyboarding process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../resources_page.rst:144
msgid "Link: https://gumroad.com/l/PtMtm"
msgstr "Länk: https://gumroad.com/l/PtMtm"

#: ../../resources_page.rst:147
msgid "Pre-installed Python Plugins"
msgstr "Förinstallerade Python-insticksprogram"

#: ../../resources_page.rst:149
msgid ""
"Krita's capabilities can be enhanced by using specific plugins. This list "
"will present the plugins that come with Krita by default, as well as other "
"plugins made by the community. If you would like to learn more about how you "
"can make your own plugin, visit the :ref:`krita_python_plugin_howto` area."
msgstr ""

#: ../../resources_page.rst:151
msgid ""
"If you want to know more about an individual plugin, you can access the "
"plugin's manual by going to :menuselection:`Settings --> Configure Krita...` "
"menu, and then choosing the Python Plugin Manager Tab. There, you can click "
"on a specific plugin, and the manual will appear in the bottom text area."
msgstr ""

#: ../../resources_page.rst:154
msgid "Assign Profile Dialog:"
msgstr "Dialogruta för tilldela profil:"

#: ../../resources_page.rst:156
msgid ""
"Allows you to assign a profile to an image instead of converting it to that "
"profile. The difference is that it allows only interpreting the colors by "
"the new profile, but not change any of the values. It can be found in :"
"menuselection:`Tools --> Assign Profile to Image...`, and will present a "
"list of profiles for the current image's color model."
msgstr ""

#: ../../resources_page.rst:159
msgid "Batch Exporter"
msgstr "Bakgrundsexport"

#: ../../resources_page.rst:161
msgid "Plugin for Game Developers and Graphic Designers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../resources_page.rst:163
msgid ""
"Allows batch export of assets to multiple sizes, file types and custom paths;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../resources_page.rst:164
msgid "Renames layers quickly with the smart rename tool;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../resources_page.rst:165
msgid "Export all layers or only selected layers;"
msgstr "Exportera alla lager eller bara markerade lager,"

#: ../../resources_page.rst:167
msgid ""
"By default, the plugin exports the images in an :file:`export` folder next "
"to the Krita document, and follows the structure of your layer stack."
msgstr ""

#: ../../resources_page.rst:171
msgid "Channels to Layers"
msgstr "Kanaler till lager"

#: ../../resources_page.rst:172
msgid ""
"Splits channels from a layer to sub-layers. To use, select the layer to "
"convert, click on :menuselection:`Tools --> Scripts --> Channels to Layers..."
"`, and choose options from the user interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../resources_page.rst:175
msgid "Color Space"
msgstr "Färgrymd"

#: ../../resources_page.rst:177
msgid ""
"Allows you to select a document and convert it's colors to a new color "
"space, like RGBA, CMYKA, L*a*b, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../resources_page.rst:180
msgid "Comics Project Management Tools"
msgstr "Projekthanteringsverktyg för tecknade serier"

#: ../../resources_page.rst:182
msgid "Aims to simplify comics creation by:"
msgstr "Har som mål att förenkla serieskapande genom att:"

#: ../../resources_page.rst:184
msgid "Giving the artist a way to organize and quickly access their pages;"
msgstr "Ge konstnären ett sätt att organisera och snabbt komma åt sina sidor,"

#: ../../resources_page.rst:185
msgid ""
"Helping the artist(s) deal with the boring bits meta data bits of a comic "
"project by giving a meta-data editor that gives suggestions, explanation and "
"occasionally a dab of humor;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../resources_page.rst:186
msgid ""
"Making export set-and-forget type of affair where a single click can export "
"to multiple formats with proper meta-data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../resources_page.rst:188
msgid ""
"Also features options to to assist exporting to specific formats, like "
"\"Advanced Comic Book Format\", CBZ or Epub."
msgstr ""

#: ../../resources_page.rst:190
msgid "To use this plugin, activate the \"Comics Manager\" Docker."
msgstr ""

#: ../../resources_page.rst:193
msgid "Document Tools"
msgstr "Dokumentverktyg"

#: ../../resources_page.rst:195
msgid ""
"Allows you to select a document and scale, crop and rotate in one action."
msgstr ""

#: ../../resources_page.rst:198
msgid "Export Layers"
msgstr "Exportera lager"

#: ../../resources_page.rst:200
msgid ""
"Allows you to select a document and export it’s layers in an ordered and "
"sensible manner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../resources_page.rst:203
msgid "Filter Manager"
msgstr "Filterhantering"

#: ../../resources_page.rst:205
msgid ""
"A plugin to enable you to select a document or one of it's layers and "
"quickly apply a filter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../resources_page.rst:208
msgid "High Pass"
msgstr "Högpass"

#: ../../resources_page.rst:210
msgid "Performs a high pass filter on the active document."
msgstr ""

#: ../../resources_page.rst:213
msgid "Krita Script Starter"
msgstr "Krita skriptstart"

#: ../../resources_page.rst:215
msgid ""
"A script that helps set up the various files that Krita expects to see when "
"it runs a script, namely:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../resources_page.rst:217
msgid "The .desktop meta data file;"
msgstr "Metadatafilen .desktop,"

#: ../../resources_page.rst:218
msgid "The package directory;"
msgstr "Paketkatalogen,"

#: ../../resources_page.rst:219
msgid "The __init__.py file;"
msgstr "Filen __init__.py,"

#: ../../resources_page.rst:220
msgid "The main python file for your package;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../resources_page.rst:221
msgid "The Manual.html file for your documentation;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../resources_page.rst:224
msgid "Last Documents Docker"
msgstr "Senaste dokumentpanel"

#: ../../resources_page.rst:226
msgid ""
"Script that shows the recently opened documents as a thumbnail image. To use "
"this, activate the \"Last Documents\" docker."
msgstr ""

#: ../../resources_page.rst:229
msgid "Mixer Slider Docker"
msgstr "Blandningsreglagepanel"

#: ../../resources_page.rst:231
msgid "Docker that allows you to choose from the gradients between two colors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../resources_page.rst:234
msgid "Palette Docker"
msgstr "Palettpanel"

#: ../../resources_page.rst:236
msgid ""
"A Docker that allows you to control palettes more easily. You can add "
"swatches, groups and export the palette settings, or even the palette itself "
"as a GIMP Palette or Inkscape SVG."
msgstr ""

#: ../../resources_page.rst:239
msgid "Photobash Images Docker"
msgstr ""

#: ../../resources_page.rst:241
msgid ""
"Simple Krita Plugin that lists the images you have on a folder you specify, "
"with the ability to filter by words in the path. To use, activate the "
"\"Photobash Images\" docker, and set the references directory. After that, "
"you can:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../resources_page.rst:243
msgid ""
"Filter images by words. Using multiple words like \"rock marble\" will show "
"all the images that have rock OR marble in the name;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../resources_page.rst:244
msgid "Scroll the pages to access more results;"
msgstr "Rulla sidorna för att komma åt fler resultat."

#: ../../resources_page.rst:245
msgid "Click on an image to create a layer, with the scale that you specify."
msgstr "Klicka på en bild för att skapa ett lager, med skalan som man anger."

#: ../../resources_page.rst:248
msgid "Python Plugin Importer"
msgstr "Python-insticksimport"

#: ../../resources_page.rst:250
msgid "Imports Python plugins from zip files."
msgstr "Importerar Python-insticksprogram från zip-filer."

#: ../../resources_page.rst:253
msgid "Quick Settings Docker"
msgstr "Dockningspanel med snabbinställningar"

#: ../../resources_page.rst:255
msgid ""
"A Docker that allows you to quickly set the opacity, flow and size from a "
"predefined list. Now, when you have a document open, and a brush selected, "
"select any of the entries in the \"Quick Settings\" docker to change them. "
"The docker doesn’t update when changing brush size any other way, so it will "
"always show the last selected change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../resources_page.rst:258
msgid "Scripter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../resources_page.rst:260
msgid ""
"A small Python scripting console, allows to write code in an editor and run "
"it, with feedback related to the output of the execution. You can also debug "
"your code using the \"Debug\" button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../resources_page.rst:263
msgid "Ten Brushes"
msgstr "Tio penslar"

#: ../../resources_page.rst:265
msgid ""
"A Script to assign presets to one of ten configurable hotkeys. To use, go "
"to :menuselection:`Tools --> Scripts --> Ten Brushes`, and a window will pop "
"up with a preset chooser and ten boxes above it. Underneath the boxes is the "
"hotkey the box is associated with."
msgstr ""

#: ../../resources_page.rst:267
msgid ""
"Customize your shortcuts by editing the configurations in :menuselection:"
"`Settings --> Configure Krita --> Keyboard Shortcuts`, and then change the "
"\"Activate Brush Preset\" actions under \"Ten Brushes\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../resources_page.rst:270
msgid "Ten Scripts"
msgstr "Tio skript"

#: ../../resources_page.rst:272
msgid ""
"Similar to Ten Brushes, allows the assign of Python scripts to one of ten "
"configurable hotkeys."
msgstr ""

#: ../../resources_page.rst:275
msgid "User-made Python Plugins"
msgstr "Användarskapade Python-insticksprogram"

#: ../../resources_page.rst:277
msgid ""
"To install and manage your plugins, see the second area of the :ref:"
"`krita_python_plugin_howto` page to know how to get Krita to recognize your "
"plugin."
msgstr ""
"För att installera och hantera insticksprogram, se den andra delen av sidan :"
"ref:`krita_python_plugin_howto` för att ta reda på hur man får Krita att "
"känna igen insticksprogrammet."

#: ../../resources_page.rst:281
msgid "AnimLayers (Animate with Layers)"
msgstr "AnimLayers (Animera med lager)"

#: ../../resources_page.rst:283
msgid ""
"Animate specific layers. You animate a specific range of layers by prefixing "
"the layer name with the same letters. For example *PL* then all the layers "
"where the name starts with *PL* will be part of the animation. In the "
"AnimLayers window you enter PL in the Key field. You can also select a layer "
"with the wanted key and press the Get key button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../resources_page.rst:285
msgid "Available here: https://github.com/thomaslynge/krita-plugins"
msgstr "Tillgänglig här: https://github.com/thomaslynge/krita-plugins"

